From 049615e9f94850e6009d6436df960bac5b77ed34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:12:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): #3840 review: live-turn record means
 running; no stray marker retire [daveey]

Review of #3840 at 1fed4d7e (patch-identical to c3c17afa):
1. settle_prompt_state drops the live-turn record where it clears running; the
   settle() pop stays. A refusal right after a turn ends behaves as a normal one.
2. Direct-call tests for every guard: the kickoff's spared/normal release, the
   _notif_submit verdict reset (stale True never leaks), the agent-None branch
   (asserted before settle can mask it). T5 now calls _notif_submit and
   _run_prompt_submit directly on a real live turn's record (no faked claim).
3. The spared branch is labelled defensive: every current caller claims running
   before it submits.
4. The missing-agent refusal, agent_init_failed (prompt.submit) and
   admission_dispatch_failed (prompt.admit) wrote no marker, so they pass
   retire_marker=False: a sibling's marker survives each.
5. The "live turn lost its marker" WARNING skips a turn retiring its own marker
   in its conclusion (_turn_concluding_marker_key, set before the retire, cleared
   when the next turn records its marker); a genuinely lost marker still warns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
